# Security scanning tools for CI/CD pipeline
# This file contains tools specifically for the security job in CI workflows.
# Run `make compile` in this directory to generate pinned security.txt
#
# NOTE: These tools are ONLY used for scanning/auditing the codebase and
# its dependencies. They are NOT runtime dependencies of the application.
#
# Governance: ADR pending - Security toolchain must be locked and deterministic.
# See .github/workflows/security-unified.yml for security job usage.

# Static security analyzer for Python code
# Detects common security issues (hardcoded passwords, SQL injection, etc.)
bandit[toml]>=1.9,<2

# Dependency vulnerability scanner
# Audits requirements files for known CVEs via PyPI advisory database
# This is the SOLE governed blocking dependency scanner for CI
pip-audit>=2.10,<3

# Transitive cachecontrol[filecache] dependency; floor kept explicit for GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964.
msgpack>=1.2.1,<2

# Safety was removed from the security toolchain (March 2026):
# - Safety pulls nltk as a transitive dependency, triggering security alerts
# - pip-audit provides equivalent CVE/advisory scanning via PyPI database
# - Removing Safety simplifies the toolchain and eliminates alert noise
# To re-enable Safety, add it here and update security-unified.yml workflow.
